{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Snowplow collector as self-describing events, whose schemas come from the tracking plan."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SnowplowEncoding"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","title":"SnowplowEncoding","externalID":"SnowplowEncoding"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-Snowplow","title":"Sending to Snowplow","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowSetupError"]},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder"]},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError"]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"text":" makes an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"text":") for a Snowplow pipeline in one call. It checks the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"collector’s URL, the Iglu vendor and the app ID, and posts to the collector’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/tp2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" endpoint with a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder"},{"text":". It splits each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch to the limits of Snowplow’s own mobile trackers (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"text":"): 25","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events and 40,000 bytes a request, with a larger event, of up to 150,000 bytes, in a request of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its own. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"included, makes no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and reports any other status. No trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leaves this module out;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"import it on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A collector takes events from anyone who can reach it, so there is no key or secret, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination builds on every platform: an app sends to the collector directly."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import SnowplowEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let snowplow = try HTTPDestination.snowplow(","    collector: collector,  \/\/ https:\/\/collector.example.com","    vendor: \"com.example\",  \/\/ the Iglu vendor the plan is exported under","    appID: \"shop-ios\",","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: snowplow)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The factory throws ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowSetupError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for a collector URL that isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"https","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", that has no host,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a user name, a query or a fragment, or that already ends in the endpoint; for a vendor Iglu","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doesn’t take; and for an empty app ID or one longer than 255 UTF-16 code units.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Schemas-from-the-tracking-plan","text":"Schemas from the tracking plan","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each event is a self-describing event: its data comes with the Iglu URI of the schema it must"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"match, and Snowplow’s pipeline validates it against that schema before loading it. The URI is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"named after the event and its version, under the vendor the destination is given:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["iglu:<vendor>\/<name>\/jsonschema\/<version>-0-0"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Version N of an event is SchemaVer ","type":"text"},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and events always name it. Raising an event’s version","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a breaking change, which is SchemaVer’s MODEL. The export compares each event with the newest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schema of its version the registry holds, by what the two mean rather than their bytes, as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plan’s own check does:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event that hasn’t changed keeps its published file, and nothing is written."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A breaking change at the same version, such as a property made required, is refused: raise the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s version."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A compatible change, such as an optional property added, is an ADDITION. For Iglu Server the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"export writes it as ","type":"text"},{"code":"N-0-1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then ","type":"text"},{"code":"N-0-2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", each listing the earlier ones in ","type":"text"},{"code":"$supersedes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Snowplow validates events naming ","type":"text"},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" against the newest, so a release already in users’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hands keeps validating. Superseding needs Iglu Server 0.11.0 or later and Enrich 3.8.0 or later.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A static repository doesn’t support it: it would validate those events against ","type":"text"},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" alone,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so for one the export refuses the change, and the event needs a new version.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Write the registry from the plan with ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan.writeIgluRegistry(to:vendor:registry:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"iglu <vendor> server|static <registry-directory>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" command of the tracking plan’s executable, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"code":"export-tracking-plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"--iglu-vendor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"--iglu-registry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Then publish it with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"igluctl","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" before the release that sends the events.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event name Iglu takes holds only ASCII letters, digits, "},{"code":"-","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"_","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the version must be 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or more. The encoder skips every record of an event that breaks either rule, and logs a notice for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each such event of the plan when the destination is made. The export refuses such an event too."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"What-Snowplow-receives","text":"What Snowplow receives","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each request is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"payload_data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" 1-0-4 array of events, one per record. Every event has:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ue"},{"text":": a self-describing event, with its data in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ue_pr"},{"text":" as JSON text;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"eid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dtm"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ttm"},{"text":", the record’s timestamp in milliseconds, so Snowplow’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"derived_tstamp"},{"text":" is when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the event was tracked;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"aid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the app ID; "},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the platform; "},{"code":"tv","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; and "},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"0.0.0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No "},{"code":"stm","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent: a retried request sends the same body again, so a sent time would be the first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attempt’s, and Snowplow would move the event later by however long the retries took."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The standard context, when the record has it, goes in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"co"},{"type":"text","text":" as Snowplow’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mobile_context"},{"type":"text","text":" 1-0-3"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(the operating system, Apple as the manufacturer, the device model, the network type and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"language) and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application"},{"type":"text","text":" 1-0-0 (the app’s version and build). The platform is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mob"},{"type":"text","text":" for a phone,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pad, watch or Vision Pro, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tv"},{"type":"text","text":" for an Apple TV, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pc"},{"type":"text","text":" for a Mac and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app"},{"type":"text","text":" for a record with no device."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Only-the-session-identifies-a-record","text":"Only the session identifies a record","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, from the sessions enricher, is its "},{"code":"sid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", Snowplow’s "},{"code":"domain_sessionid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing else identifies it. No "},{"code":"duid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"uid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"nuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"tnuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent, no "},{"code":"client_session","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entity (its "},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lasts across sessions), and no IDFV, IDFA or other device identifier. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent either. A record with no session, from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker without the sessions enricher, is sent without a "},{"code":"sid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; a record a store recovered after a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relaunch keeps its session and its "},{"code":"sid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Snowplow’s mobile data models"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read a session from the "},{"code":"client_session","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entity, so set the unified package’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"snowplow__session_identifiers","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"code":"[{\"schema\": \"atomic\", \"field\": \"domain_sessionid\"}]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for these"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The collector would give each device an identifier of its own: it sets an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sp"},{"type":"text","text":" cookie, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps and sends back, and records the request’s IP address. Every request carries"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SP-Anonymous: *"},{"type":"text","text":", so the collector sets and reads no cookie, records "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"network_userid"},{"type":"text","text":" as all"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"zeros, and records no IP address or forwarding header fields."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Records-left-out","text":"Records left out","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose event name Iglu doesn’t take, or whose version is below 1;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose timestamp falls outside the years 0 to 9999, which Snowplow’s enrichment fails;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose JSON is over 150,000 bytes, which the smallest of a pipeline’s streams, SQS’s 192 kB,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"might not take with the request around it."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The destination reports each as ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose reason is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"What-the-collector-doesnt-report","text":"What the collector doesn’t report","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The collector answers 200 to every request it can read and validates nothing. Snowplow checks the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events later, in enrichment. An event whose data its schema rejects, whose schema the pipeline’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Iglu resolver can’t find, or that is larger than the pipeline’s stream takes, becomes a failed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event: it is kept apart and never reaches the warehouse, though the destination counted it as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered. Publish each schema before the release that sends it, and watch the pipeline’s failed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events after a change to the plan. Snowplow’s resolver caches schemas, for 10 minutes by default,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so a schema published after the first event that names it can still be missed for that long.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Snowplow doesn’t remove duplicates as events arrive. A record is sent more than once when a request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is retried after the collector stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a cancelled"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch again, and when a store redelivers records after a relaunch. Each copy keeps its "},{"code":"eid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Snowplow’s data models, which deduplicate on "},{"code":"event_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", count it once."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what Snowplow receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/snowplowencoding"]}],"references":{"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding":{"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding","title":"SnowplowEncoding","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Snowplow collector as self-describing events, whose schemas come from the tracking plan."}]},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A destination that sends batches to the Snowplow collector at ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collector"},{"text":", as self-describing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events whose schemas are ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":"’s under ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vendor"},{"text":", from the app ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appID"},{"text":", through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transport"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"retrying a send that fails for now with the waits of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appid:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","type":"topic","title":"snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"snowplow","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"collector","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"URL","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials3URLV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"vendor","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"appID","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"plan","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrackingPlan","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"transport","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"backoff","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clock","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Clock","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnowplowSetupError","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SnowplowEncoding0A10SetupErrorO"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnowplowBatchEncoder","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SnowplowEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/SnowplowEncodingError":{"abstract":[{"text":"Why ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requests as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends nothing for the batch.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SnowplowEncodingError"}],"title":"SnowplowEncodingError","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind"